<description>
Paint the even square-distance rings around the solid foreground cross yellow.

Input structure:
- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.
- The foreground is exactly one full row and one full column crossing each other.
- Yellow is absent from the input and is the output fill color.

Rule:
- Locate the unique solid foreground row and column, whose intersection is the ring center.
- For every background pixel, compute its Chebyshev distance from that center.
- Recolor background pixels with even Chebyshev distance to yellow.
- Keep the foreground cross unchanged.

Key insight:
- The output is not drawn from separate quadrant patterns; it is one set of alternating square rings centered on the cross intersection.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "background pixels around a single solid foreground row/column cross",
  "transform": "recolor to yellow each background pixel whose Chebyshev distance from the cross intersection is even; preserve the foreground cross and odd-distance background pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10-20 rows x 10-20 cols, always square [observed]
  colors:
    background: BLACK (0) [observed]
    foreground: GREEN (3) [observed], exactly 1 non-bg color
    yellow: absent from input, used only in output
  cross:
    structure: exactly one full-width row + one full-height column, all fg color
    center: intersection at (cr, cc); not on any edge (1 <= cr <= H-2, 1 <= cc <= W-2)
    min_edge_distance: >=3, ensures >=3 visible complete rings [observed]
    foreground_is_exactly_cross: all fg pixels lie on the cross row/col, no extras
  transform:
    for each bg pixel, compute Chebyshev distance d = max(|r-cr|, |c-cc|)
    if d is even, recolor to YELLOW; if odd, keep bg
    cross pixels unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input is trivial, no inversion needed)
  steps:
    1. pick N in [10..20]; create NxN grid filled with BLACK
    2. pick cr in [3..N-4], cc in [3..N-4] to ensure min_edge_distance >= 3
    3. fill row cr and column cc with GREEN
    4. verify no yellow in input (trivially satisfied)
```
